      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e but I realized that rand init uses panic!\n\nNote that `panic!` doesn\u0027t use the logger (`log::{warn,error,...}`) but accesses the UART directly through `eprintln!` so that should be fine.\n\n\u003e in the upcoming changes moves the extraction of FDT location to `platform::init()`\n\nSo you want to locate the DT (completely unnecessary to pvmfw\u0027s bring up) before `log` has been configured or the stack guard initialized? That doesn\u0027t sound like the right order of execution to me.\n\n\u003e So either the extaction has to refactored a bit or we leave the name\n\nI\u0027d recommend reworking the code to properly dissociate low-level bring up work of `vmbase` clients (`rust_entry()`) from high-level functional operations such as locating a DT.\n\nNote that this is more fundamental than just a function name.",
