      "message": "\u003e Locating and parsing configurations are platfrom dependent.\n\nTo be clear, I\u0027m not contesting this but only saying that not _all_ platform code should run at the point where `platform::init()` (now `init_console()`) gets called.\n\n\u003e we need some form of abstraction that we are lacking\n\nAgreed!\n\n\u003e Which could be a duplication of code considering that we will also want that in vmbase\n\nSure, and it should therefore probably go in `libvmbase`. My point was simply that locating the DT (or similar) is high-level enough that it doesn\u0027t have to happen from `rust_entry()` and, instead, could be called from clients when they actually need it. As a somewhat related case, see how our PCI/VirtIO drivers get brought up by pvmfw and Rialto.",
